{"model":"gpt-4.1-nano","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"I'm preparing a short teaching note for a chat application. Explain in two sentences why an append-only event log differs from a derived context view. Use a concrete chat-history example."},{"role":"assistant","content":"An append-only event log in a chat app records every message as a distinct, immutable event, like a timeline of \"User A sent 'hello'\" followed by \"User B sent 'hi'\". In contrast, a derived context view is a curated representation of this data, perhaps showing only the last 10 messages in a specific conversation, generated on demand from the underlying log."},{"role":"user","content":"Using your example, give one sentence explaining why rendering that saved log offline should not contact the model again."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Since the append-only event log is a complete, immutable record of all past messages, rendering it offline simply involves replaying these saved events directly, without needing to consult any external model for new or modified data."}]}
